Participant: Participant A-03 (synthetic portfolio administrator)
Portfolio: Juniper Works / Product Alpha Q3
Interview date: 2026-07-13

Q: What repeated work would you hand to the product?
A: "Every Monday I recreate the same routing rule for each new project." A-03
could copy a prior rule, but had to reopen it, change the owner, and re-enable
notifications one workspace at a time. They wanted a template that previews
which settings will be inherited before applying it.

Q: Where did permissions become confusing?
A: The participant could create a template but not publish it to other admins.
The error message said access was required without naming the missing role or
the person who could approve it. A role matrix at the point of action would
have prevented a support request.

Q: What result would demonstrate value in the first session?
A: Applying one approved template to a new project and then seeing the first
routed item arrive. A-03 did not need a dashboard first; they needed proof
that a repeated administrative task would stay repeated correctly.

Initial codes: admin automation; permissions comprehension; time-to-first-value.
Researcher note: A template request includes both speed and safeguards. Code
preview/rollback needs separately if future evidence names them.
